00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:51.767
This is a proactive approach instead of a reactive

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:52.300
approach.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:54.634
This has to do with

00:12:55.667 --> 00:12:59.367
K Lupa 22 shipyard and terminal area policy B.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:03.033
At the last comprehensive plan meeting, the word potential

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:04.767
was added,

00:13:06.767 --> 00:13:10.033
saying potential significant VOC emissions, which

00:13:10.066 --> 00:13:13.967
acknowledges the current empty tanks could become active as long

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:16.166
as they're licensed to. This is great.

00:13:16.333 --> 00:13:19.700
I thank both the CBC in planning for adding that.

00:13:20.667 --> 00:13:24.467
From a functional perspective, this does very little unless we

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:26.900
add some proactive language with it.

00:13:26.934 --> 00:13:30.900
For example, in correspondence with the DEP, I asked whether the DEP

00:13:30.967 --> 00:13:34.300
or CDC forecasts future emissions from bulk

00:13:34.667 --> 00:13:38.200
petroleum storage terminals using historical data.

00:13:38.734 --> 00:13:42.700
Her reply, "No, the DEP does not forecast emissions.

00:13:43.367 --> 00:13:46.700
Instead, permits are based on a facility's maximum

00:13:47.133 --> 00:13:48.300
potential to emit."

00:13:49.166 --> 00:13:52.667
The term potential to emit is a formal regulatory

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:56.166
concept used by the main DEP. It is not a

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:59.834
forecast or an estimate of future conditions, but a legally defined

00:13:59.967 --> 00:14:03.066
maximum level of emissions allowed under a facility's permit.

00:14:03.634 --> 00:14:06.467
This is really important to understand if you truly want to help people

00:14:07.266 --> 00:14:10.767
or keep people safe. In the last few years, Sunoco was operating at

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:14.467
30% of their legal potential to emit, again, based on

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:18.000
throughput and tank activity. These are calculated

00:14:18.033 --> 00:14:21.533
emissions from the terminal sent to the DEP every year.

00:14:21.567 --> 00:14:24.934
However, that level isn't fixed. From 2015 to

00:14:25.467 --> 00:14:29.266
2018, throughput was significantly higher, at 60%,

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:30.166
twice the amount.

00:14:30.967 --> 00:14:34.700
Concurrently, the DEP is collecting emissions samples and sending them to the

00:14:34.734 --> 00:14:38.500
CDC. This is where the data comes from, which is used to

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.567
create the charts the CDC presents at meetings.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:45.900
It is also the evidence-based data where it is rooted in that,

00:14:46.467 --> 00:14:49.834
which is proposed policy that it talks about in the plan.

00:14:50.767 --> 00:14:54.700
If the planning decisions are informed by emissions that are measured with sampling

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:58.667
during low throughput, then the facility later operates

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:02.600
closer to its permitted maximum potential to emit.

00:15:02.667 --> 00:15:06.200
You can see how the term evidence-based becomes really spongy,

00:15:07.033 --> 00:15:10.200
which can be dangerous for any future residents of that property,

00:15:10.834 --> 00:15:13.433
totally misrepresenting reality.

00:15:13.734 --> 00:15:14.433
30 seconds.

00:15:14.667 --> 00:15:18.533
What I suggest, after the line that ends with "Demonstrate acceptable

00:15:18.667 --> 00:15:22.433
conditions for long-term occupancy," add the following,

00:15:23.133 --> 00:15:26.500
"The evaluation must incorporate

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:31.166
maximum potential to emit values for ensuring

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:33.567
safety for the long term."

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:38.800
Those words, maximum potential emissions, are exactly as the DEP

00:15:38.867 --> 00:15:40.200
worded it

00:15:41.066 --> 00:15:42.900
and how they look in the future.

00:15:43.066 --> 00:15:44.600
Time.

00:15:44.634 --> 00:15:44.967
Thank you.

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:46.900
Thank you very much.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:49.967
You know what?

00:15:50.867 --> 00:15:54.734
We're not going to do clapping or booing or finger

00:15:54.867 --> 00:15:58.767
snapping or hissing because one,

00:15:58.967 --> 00:15:59.266
it's

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:04.400
going to take us a long time to get through, and two, it does

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:08.266
kind of maybe discourage people who, if they hear clapping for one

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:11.567
kind of opinion, might not be encouraged to offer a different

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:14.967
opinion. So I'll just put that out there.

00:16:16.467 --> 00:16:17.467
One thing that I also

00:16:18.567 --> 00:16:22.367
thought I'd told you every rule that was ever written, but to

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:26.266
keep in mind is that on a particular subject, you can

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:30.300
comment once. So just making sure people know that,

00:16:30.367 --> 00:16:30.634
too.

00:16:31.467 --> 00:16:34.600
All right. If there is anyone else who wants to make a public comment

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:39.266
on or off the agenda. I don't see anyone.

00:16:39.367 --> 00:16:40.233
That comment period-

00:16:40.266 --> 00:16:41.066
No, she's up.

00:16:41.066 --> 00:16:44.266
Up, up, up. Almost. Come on, don't be shy, all y'all.

00:16:44.467 --> 00:16:45.567
Come on down.

00:16:47.066 --> 00:16:47.767
Make a line-

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:48.467
Make sure you-

00:16:48.467 --> 00:16:49.433
... if there's going to be multiple.

00:16:50.233 --> 00:16:53.767
Okay. Or ask if anybody... Help me keep track of if

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:55.634
anybody's there.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:56.767
Yeah.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.767
Hi, Pam Thomas, Alder Street, and

00:17:04.834 --> 00:17:08.567
21-year resident and 14-year manufacturing

00:17:08.667 --> 00:17:11.567
company in South Portland co-owner.

00:17:15.166 --> 00:17:19.000
Look across the harbor. Portland has a sliver of land with

00:17:19.066 --> 00:17:23.000
high-rises hovering over it, shading the waterfront trail and

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:26.867
shoreline every afternoon. Cruise ships block the

00:17:26.934 --> 00:17:30.800
wind for small boats and kids as teens and adults and kids try to

00:17:30.867 --> 00:17:32.600
reach the harbor without an engine.

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:36.934
On our side of the harbor, once the tanks are gone

00:17:37.667 --> 00:17:41.000
and the contaminated land is cleared, cleaned, excuse me,

00:17:41.567 --> 00:17:45.467
imagine open space. Imagine enhanced public

00:17:45.734 --> 00:17:49.567
access to the waterfront. Imagine families having elbow

00:17:49.634 --> 00:17:52.000
room to blanket on the grass and picnic.

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:56.567
This prime, unobstructed waterfront

00:17:56.634 --> 00:18:00.433
location should be shared with all residents

00:18:00.567 --> 00:18:03.734
and visitors, not just the wealthy few.

00:18:04.567 --> 00:18:07.200
A sliver of land is not going to cut it.

00:18:09.166 --> 00:18:12.734
Fort Williams in Cape Elizabeth is 90 acres.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.533
Bug Light Park is less than nine acres.

00:18:17.533 --> 00:18:21.100
I encourage you to bring back K Lupa 27 as the Eastern

00:18:21.166 --> 00:18:25.133
Marine Protection Area. I request that you downgrade

00:18:25.166 --> 00:18:28.967
the growth designation to limited or conservation.

00:18:29.667 --> 00:18:33.634
Let's permit a resilient park in this flood zone rather

00:18:33.667 --> 00:18:37.467
than high-rise condos and businesses that we will eventually have to

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:41.433
bail out.Let's give the SOS group time

00:18:41.467 --> 00:18:45.300
to organize and seek funding from national organizations for a

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:49.033
resilient park. Please slow down and think

00:18:49.066 --> 00:18:49.800
big.

00:18:51.233 --> 00:18:54.934
As taxpayers, we already see and understand the

00:18:55.033 --> 00:18:58.967
pressure on our aging water treatment plant, our schools, our public

00:18:59.033 --> 00:19:02.700
transportation, our fire rescue services, our boat

00:19:02.767 --> 00:19:05.734
launch, our beach, our roads, and in particular, Broadway.

00:19:06.533 --> 00:19:09.934
When Ferry Village floods with sea level rise, we will be

00:19:10.033 --> 00:19:13.834
overwhelmed and out of money, and as a result, you will increase

00:19:13.934 --> 00:19:17.934
taxes on all residents because of the impact of building in a

00:19:18.033 --> 00:19:21.400
flood zone at the tip of a peninsula

00:19:21.834 --> 00:19:25.367
with a drawbridge adjacent to toxic fumes.

00:19:27.133 --> 00:19:29.834
I ask you this, please Google an article.

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:34.100
It's by Fast Company. It's The Four Best Waterfront

00:19:34.233 --> 00:19:38.033
Parks of 2025 That Transform Shorelines into-

00:19:38.033 --> 00:19:38.100
30 seconds

00:19:38.133 --> 00:19:41.900
... City Centerpieces. Again, Fast Company article,

00:19:44.066 --> 00:19:47.934
Best Shorelines of Waterfront Parks 2025, and thank you so much.

00:19:48.033 --> 00:19:49.166
I think it will inspire you.

00:19:50.533 --> 00:19:52.400
Thank you very much, Ms. Thomas.

00:19:55.967 --> 00:19:59.033
Hello. You've heard from me before, but I don't know where I am on the

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:03.066
agenda. So my name is Leslie Gatcombe Hines,

00:20:03.133 --> 00:20:07.100
and I live at 47 Elmwood Avenue. I previously expressed my

00:20:07.133 --> 00:20:11.066
thoughts on the comprehensive plan to the council and reiterate them.

00:20:11.166 --> 00:20:14.433
I think that precious shoreline property should be reserved for marine and

00:20:14.533 --> 00:20:18.133
recreational use that unlike hotels

00:20:18.233 --> 00:20:21.467
or other businesses that could be located elsewhere.

00:20:21.934 --> 00:20:25.800
Particularly in regard to lands likely to be submerged from rising sea levels, I

00:20:25.834 --> 00:20:29.767
disagree with placing any residential or non-marine commercial buildings there.

00:20:30.533 --> 00:20:33.767
The tax base also needs to be considered, as any construction requires

00:20:33.834 --> 00:20:35.900
infrastructure, much of which is aging.

00:20:36.734 --> 00:20:40.500
For example, my street continues to be hit with a lot of runoff from higher ground

00:20:40.567 --> 00:20:44.066
water and threatened with flooding from future sea level rise,

00:20:44.934 --> 00:20:48.734
and the sewer drainage is inadequate for the task, for which I have

00:20:48.767 --> 00:20:50.767
brought to all the city authorities that I can.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:55.133
And the issue of oil tanks and past business use also needs to be addressed.

00:20:56.200 --> 00:20:59.066
About, I think it was about seven years ago when we gathered

00:20:59.867 --> 00:21:01.000
samples from the air.

00:21:02.266 --> 00:21:05.767
I brought home one of those vacuum tanks, placed it on my deck, and it just goes

00:21:06.533 --> 00:21:09.834
and took a sample of air. When I released the seal, that

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:14.166
sample was sucked in. The air was found to be contaminated with volatile

00:21:14.233 --> 00:21:15.166
organic chemicals.

00:21:16.567 --> 00:21:20.400
I have lived in South Portland most of my adult life, 21 years in my

00:21:20.433 --> 00:21:20.967
current home,

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:24.133
and I'm being treated right now for cancer.

00:21:25.233 --> 00:21:26.767
I had genetic testing that can

00:21:28.767 --> 00:21:32.266
determine that my type of cancer is not genetic, therefore it must be

00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:32.934
environmental.

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:37.400
So I am concerned with the EPA maps which show my neighborhood as being at

00:21:37.533 --> 00:21:38.734
moderate cancer risk.

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:43.100
Many cancers are environmentally caused, and we need to do what we can to mitigate

00:21:43.133 --> 00:21:43.667
that risk.

00:21:44.533 --> 00:21:47.567
And finally, I also had advocated that all South Portland residents should have

00:21:47.667 --> 00:21:51.367
easy walking access to green space, and this is important for both the physical and

00:21:51.433 --> 00:21:53.834
mental health of our inhabitants and wildlife.

00:21:54.634 --> 00:21:57.634
South Portland has a good environmental record, and I would like to see that

00:21:57.667 --> 00:21:58.200
continue.

00:21:59.066 --> 00:22:00.967
I'm here for the planet. Thank you.

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:03.300
Thank you very much.

00:22:06.533 --> 00:22:09.900
Hello, my name is Edward Reiner. I live on 25 Ballard Street.

00:22:11.467 --> 00:22:15.266
I too, am in cancer treatment right now

00:22:15.867 --> 00:22:17.634
for bladder cancer. My

00:22:18.867 --> 00:22:22.500
house is at the end of Elm Street. We're about 700 feet from the

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:24.667
Global and Sprague tanks.

00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:29.467
I've recently been interviewed by The Boston Globe about the hazards in that

00:22:29.533 --> 00:22:33.433
neighborhood. One of my conclusions was that there should be

00:22:33.467 --> 00:22:37.467
epidemiological studies so we actually know how many people are

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:38.300
being sickened.

00:22:39.767 --> 00:22:42.867
I'm reminded of Tom Blake's, the

00:22:43.734 --> 00:22:47.533
previous mayor, Tom Blake's efforts in the tar sands and

00:22:47.567 --> 00:22:47.734
how

00:22:48.667 --> 00:22:52.634
valiantly he fought to protect the public

00:22:52.700 --> 00:22:56.567
health, and it resulted in a positive decision for the Clear

00:22:56.700 --> 00:23:00.433
Skies ordinance. I was inspired by that, knowing that he

00:23:00.467 --> 00:23:02.433
himself felt he grew up

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:07.367
and was sickened by... lifelong resident on the waterfront here.

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:10.133
So my conclusions about

00:23:11.033 --> 00:23:14.967
the property near Bug Light is that before anything is built,

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:20.700
the health hazards, the air quality has to be considered

00:23:20.734 --> 00:23:24.600
before going forward, as well as the consideration we

00:23:24.667 --> 00:23:28.133
just heard about the floodplain being a limiting factor.

00:23:29.567 --> 00:23:32.867
And I'm highly in favor of

00:23:33.066 --> 00:23:35.200
waterfront access and open space.

00:23:35.266 --> 00:23:37.967
That's what we need in an urban area.

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:41.600
And one of my reflections on living in South Portland, it's a very

00:23:41.700 --> 00:23:45.066
livable city other than our problems with air quality.

00:23:47.033 --> 00:23:50.800
So keeping green space and recreational opportunities,

00:23:51.767 --> 00:23:55.700
I fly kites with my granddaughters at Bug Light, and I

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:59.400
would like them to be able to feel that there's some nature beyond Bug Light

00:23:59.467 --> 00:24:00.834
that's just nine acres. So

00:24:01.667 --> 00:24:04.967
I'm asking you to consider to go slowly and

00:24:05.266 --> 00:24:06.100
consider those

00:24:07.400 --> 00:24:11.367
considerations of air quality and the floodplain

00:24:11.667 --> 00:24:15.367
and open space. I think those all have to be taken into consideration.

00:24:16.033 --> 00:24:16.333
Thank you.

00:24:17.166 --> 00:24:18.300
Thank you very much.

00:24:20.333 --> 00:24:22.800
My name is Carolyn Foley. I live on the high ground by Willard Beach.

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:25.400
With the flooding, you guys are welcome to come to my house.

00:24:25.767 --> 00:24:28.066
It's only 1,000 square feet, but you're welcome to come and stay with me.

00:24:29.066 --> 00:24:33.033
I am a biker and a pedestrian, and I fear that all the extra people

00:24:33.066 --> 00:24:34.166
and all the extra cars

00:24:34.967 --> 00:24:37.000
are going to cause more safety issues.

00:24:37.066 --> 00:24:40.967
Right now, a 10-year-old can barely get across Broadway, so the traffic is

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:41.967
just absolutely horrible.

00:24:43.166 --> 00:24:44.734
I bike. I've been biking

00:24:46.066 --> 00:24:47.734
for 40 years or so

00:24:48.567 --> 00:24:51.700
So it's not a problem, but people who are inexperienced might not be able to bike

00:24:51.767 --> 00:24:55.567
on Broadway anymore, might not be able to get across the street, especially with

00:24:55.934 --> 00:24:59.834
SMCC cars and the kids who don't really care because it's not their neighborhood.

00:25:00.934 --> 00:25:04.867
I just think that with adding so many people into

00:25:04.900 --> 00:25:07.533
that area and so many cars, it's just going to be really an issue.

00:25:08.333 --> 00:25:09.967
I don't know how you're going to plan on doing that.

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:13.900
Maybe we can start a boat ferry ride across the harbor so that people who work

00:25:13.934 --> 00:25:15.700
in Portland don't have to travel all the way around.

00:25:16.233 --> 00:25:19.433
Traffic is already really tough at rush hour traffic.

00:25:20.033 --> 00:25:22.100
I'm sure that all you guys know that because you all live here.

00:25:23.667 --> 00:25:27.567
I also want to know who is going to benefit from the monies, from the finances

00:25:27.634 --> 00:25:31.433
from building these things. Is it only going to be the people who are

00:25:31.467 --> 00:25:35.166
building it and are selling it at high prices even though there's going to be some

00:25:35.233 --> 00:25:38.600
affordable housing of like $600,000? So that's it.

00:25:39.934 --> 00:25:41.000
Thank you very much.

00:25:47.533 --> 00:25:49.834
Hi there. My name is Milo Small.

00:25:50.867 --> 00:25:52.834
I live at 41 Pier Street

00:25:53.767 --> 00:25:54.867
over in Ferry Village.

00:25:57.166 --> 00:25:58.500
I don't have a speech

00:26:00.567 --> 00:26:02.133
prepared. These are just my thoughts.

00:26:03.066 --> 00:26:06.934
I've lived in that neighborhood for my whole

00:26:06.967 --> 00:26:07.367
life.

00:26:08.233 --> 00:26:09.967
I've inherited this house from my aunt.

00:26:10.567 --> 00:26:13.600
She passed away from cancer at 61.

00:26:15.767 --> 00:26:16.200
And

00:26:20.333 --> 00:26:23.867
if the City of South Portland knows that they're

00:26:23.934 --> 00:26:27.834
building within a flood zone, my question is: Why is that

00:26:27.967 --> 00:26:29.100
even a consideration?

00:26:30.533 --> 00:26:33.266
And what is the goal for adding this infrastructure?

00:26:35.533 --> 00:26:39.467
I plan on living in this house and in this neighborhood for the rest of my life,

00:26:40.567 --> 00:26:42.433
and to know that I

00:26:43.567 --> 00:26:46.467
run past these tanks every single morning,

00:26:47.367 --> 00:26:48.667
and to know that they're

00:26:49.967 --> 00:26:52.734
actively contributing to my risk of cancer

00:26:53.934 --> 00:26:54.333
is

00:26:55.266 --> 00:26:55.934
devastating.

00:26:57.500 --> 00:26:58.433
I want to live here.

00:26:59.533 --> 00:27:00.834
We all know the housing market,

00:27:03.900 --> 00:27:06.967
of affording a place to live and move.

00:27:07.934 --> 00:27:09.166
My family lives here.

00:27:11.734 --> 00:27:12.934
This is where I want to be,

00:27:13.767 --> 00:27:14.233
and

00:27:17.433 --> 00:27:18.433
I'm asking

00:27:19.934 --> 00:27:22.734
the people in this room

00:27:22.867 --> 00:27:24.066
to

00:27:24.900 --> 00:27:25.433
see that.

00:27:27.500 --> 00:27:28.567
On another note,

00:27:29.734 --> 00:27:31.066
I went to

00:27:35.133 --> 00:27:39.133
a capstone research probably two years ago over

00:27:39.266 --> 00:27:42.533
in the Portland Public Library, where many

00:27:42.600 --> 00:27:45.634
colleges were presenting, and

00:27:46.634 --> 00:27:47.834
a Harvard student.

00:27:48.834 --> 00:27:51.400
They were architecture students

00:27:54.367 --> 00:27:58.333
who were trying to build infrastructure after the sea levels rise, and they

00:27:58.467 --> 00:27:59.367
had a map

00:28:00.500 --> 00:28:04.400
of Portland and South Portland, and my property happens to be on this

00:28:04.467 --> 00:28:04.767
map.

00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:09.567
And by 2050, it

00:28:09.734 --> 00:28:13.333
says the sea level will rise by 1.5 feet.

00:28:14.800 --> 00:28:17.800
By 2070, it will rise by three feet.

00:28:19.266 --> 00:28:20.667
And if this-

00:28:20.834 --> 00:28:20.834
30 seconds

00:28:20.834 --> 00:28:22.533
... infrastructure is built,

00:28:23.634 --> 00:28:25.967
what is the City of South Portland going to do

00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:27.200
after?

00:28:28.066 --> 00:28:29.634
Is it going to be demolitioned?

00:28:30.667 --> 00:28:31.634
The neighborhood,

00:28:32.667 --> 00:28:34.066
there's just going to be buildings

00:28:35.934 --> 00:28:37.867
submerged in three feet of water.

00:28:39.100 --> 00:28:42.867
That doesn't sound, in terms of longevity,

00:28:43.233 --> 00:28:45.567
these buildings should last for more than

00:28:48.467 --> 00:28:49.834
30 years, 40 years.

00:28:50.200 --> 00:28:51.333
Time.

00:28:53.367 --> 00:28:53.700
Thank you.

00:28:54.066 --> 00:28:55.300
Thank you very much.

00:28:57.967 --> 00:29:00.433
Okay, coming on down.

00:29:08.433 --> 00:29:08.700
Hey, everyone.

00:29:10.200 --> 00:29:13.667
So good evening. My name is Jeremy Naden, and I live at Clinton Street.

00:29:14.266 --> 00:29:18.200
November 2024 election, voters

00:29:18.266 --> 00:29:22.033
added Section 204.2 to the charter, so Bug Light, Mill Creek, and

00:29:22.066 --> 00:29:25.567
Hinckley Parks can't be sold or traded away without a referendum.

00:29:26.200 --> 00:29:28.867
This protection only exists because residents brought it.

00:29:29.333 --> 00:29:32.900
It keeps Bug Light from being sold. It doesn't keep it from being encircled.

00:29:33.367 --> 00:29:37.200
Bug Light sits in between rising water on one side and proposed

00:29:37.266 --> 00:29:39.734
residential rezoning up to six stories on the other.

00:29:40.333 --> 00:29:44.233
Prior waterfront residential proposal was withdrawn after sustained opposition,

00:29:44.700 --> 00:29:48.200
but opposition has continued in the thousands through petition signatures

00:29:48.233 --> 00:29:49.467
validated by the city clerk.

00:29:50.500 --> 00:29:54.400
The 2040 comprehensive plan has been in progress for years, but the ground

00:29:54.433 --> 00:29:58.100
has shifted since. LD 2003 in 2022

00:29:58.467 --> 00:30:01.967
and LD 1829 in 2025 changed what a city

00:30:02.033 --> 00:30:04.934
controls once it adopts growth designations.

00:30:05.700 --> 00:30:07.934
Tonight, I want to name three gaps in the plan as written.

00:30:08.834 --> 00:30:12.467
Who pays? South Portland sewer rates are set to rise 22%, as

00:30:12.533 --> 00:30:14.934
reported every year for three years,

00:30:15.734 --> 00:30:18.100
with about $50 million needed in wastewater work.

00:30:18.634 --> 00:30:22.033
Broadway already carries 24,000 vehicles a day through

00:30:22.333 --> 00:30:22.934
bottlenecks

00:30:24.200 --> 00:30:27.567
with no funded relief. Growth without funded infrastructure shifts

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:30.266
those costs onto the residents already here.

00:30:31.266 --> 00:30:35.166
Environmental sea level rise, we heard about projections up

00:30:35.233 --> 00:30:37.967
to as high as eight to 8.8 feet by 2120.

00:30:38.567 --> 00:30:42.433
Emissions concerns persist. These impact the same

00:30:42.467 --> 00:30:44.533
land the plan designates for growth.

00:30:45.433 --> 00:30:49.266
And third, process. Residents have been providing input to this plan since

00:30:49.367 --> 00:30:52.967
2022, myself included. A plan shaped by three years of

00:30:53.066 --> 00:30:57.000
resident input should not be adopted without a fresh read against the modified

00:30:57.133 --> 00:31:00.767
state laws that will actually govern it.Residents have shown up,

00:31:01.166 --> 00:31:02.767
signed, spoken, and paid attention.

00:31:02.834 --> 00:31:06.367
We deserve answers on the record before the vote, not after it.

00:31:07.166 --> 00:31:10.834
I'd also ask the council to be alert to the broader pressure this plan sits

00:31:10.867 --> 00:31:14.834
within. Regional business groups are on the record advocating to shift

00:31:14.900 --> 00:31:17.667
land use authority away from local governments.

00:31:18.467 --> 00:31:22.266
So my ask is narrow and concrete. Amend the plan to remove or

00:31:22.367 --> 00:31:26.233
defer the eastern waterfront growth designations while key concerns

00:31:26.266 --> 00:31:30.066
are addressed, and delay the vote long enough to reassess how the

00:31:30.100 --> 00:31:33.300
main growth laws actually apply to what we are about to adopt.

00:31:33.967 --> 00:31:37.867
Hard things can be accomplished. In 2014, the city won a federal lawsuit over

00:31:37.900 --> 00:31:41.800
the Clear Skies Ordinance. In decades past, Cape Elizabeth bought Fort

00:31:41.867 --> 00:31:43.800
Williams. Portland preserved the-

00:31:43.867 --> 00:31:43.967
30 seconds

00:31:43.967 --> 00:31:47.800
... Eastern Promenade. We owe the residents already here a plan that holds

00:31:47.900 --> 00:31:51.300
up, not one that leaves them asking for the next 15 years

00:31:51.800 --> 00:31:52.800
what it should answer now.

00:31:53.667 --> 00:31:54.033
Thank you.

00:31:54.700 --> 00:31:55.767
Thank you very much.

00:31:56.767 --> 00:31:59.333
Is there anyone else who would like to make a comment now?

00:32:02.266 --> 00:32:05.867
All right. You're absolutely sure? I have this little hammer.

00:32:07.000 --> 00:32:07.033
No.

00:32:07.100 --> 00:32:10.600
All right. We're going to close this public comment.

00:32:11.767 --> 00:32:13.767
There will be more opportunities.

00:32:15.767 --> 00:32:17.166
Let's move to public hearings-

00:32:17.200 --> 00:32:17.734
Questions.

00:32:17.900 --> 00:32:20.000
Oh, we do have questions to answer. I know.

00:32:20.066 --> 00:32:21.467
I guess I'd look to the planning director.

00:32:21.500 --> 00:32:25.166
I know you've been taking copious notes and are planning to provide answers.

00:32:25.233 --> 00:32:28.934
I don't know if any might be covered in your presentation too, but feel free to

00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:30.133
address the ones that you heard.

00:32:30.400 --> 00:32:33.266
Well, I have a few direct questions since they're all comp plan related.

00:32:33.300 --> 00:32:36.367
Do you want me to bundle these with the later comp plan questions?

00:32:36.900 --> 00:32:38.500
I don't know if those folks will stick around.

00:32:38.967 --> 00:32:41.166
Why don't we try it right this second?

00:32:45.500 --> 00:32:47.734
Milana Vito, the planning director.

00:32:48.166 --> 00:32:51.367
I caught three specific questions that were raised.

00:32:51.400 --> 00:32:51.900
The first

00:32:53.200 --> 00:32:55.000
was who benefits from the buildings?

00:32:55.066 --> 00:32:58.734
I think the context there was the buildings that would be allowed if we adopt a

00:32:58.800 --> 00:32:59.066
growth

00:33:00.400 --> 00:33:04.066
designation and then adopt the zoning, and then proposals are

00:33:04.100 --> 00:33:06.233
submitted, and they meet the standards that are proposed.

00:33:06.634 --> 00:33:10.634
Who would benefit from the profit, I guess, from those buildings or

00:33:10.667 --> 00:33:12.033
the finances of those buildings?

00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:16.967
And it would be the city through the collection of taxes and possibly some

00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:20.500
other things. We know, for instance, we collect fees through the development

00:33:20.634 --> 00:33:23.467
application process and the construction process.

00:33:24.533 --> 00:33:28.400
We collect sewer rates from developments at the

00:33:28.467 --> 00:33:32.433
time of connection. The plan calls for certain things like impact fees,

00:33:32.500 --> 00:33:36.133
which we're developing now based on council funding from two years

00:33:36.166 --> 00:33:39.467
prior for things like sewer traffic, and we can do other things as

00:33:39.533 --> 00:33:42.834
well. If those are in effect, we would collect all of those kinds of

00:33:42.867 --> 00:33:46.567
fees. If we implement a tax increment financing district, we could collect

00:33:47.767 --> 00:33:50.867
those sheltered dollars, which wouldn't happen otherwise.

00:33:50.967 --> 00:33:54.900
And then there's the property taxes, and if there's businesses there, there's also

00:33:54.934 --> 00:33:58.200
the personal property of those businesses that would all generate revenues for the

00:33:58.200 --> 00:33:58.400
city.

00:34:00.467 --> 00:34:03.100
So that's sort of the city side of the ledger, and I might be missing something.

00:34:03.333 --> 00:34:05.433
Scott, our finance director, can weigh in on that.

00:34:06.533 --> 00:34:10.500
But if the development is moving forward and it's a for-profit development, there's

00:34:10.500 --> 00:34:14.467
very likely, after accounting for those things, profit that's intended

00:34:14.500 --> 00:34:17.166
to be gained as well for the private parties that are making those investments.

00:34:18.600 --> 00:34:21.967
The second question I got is what is the goal with adding this infrastructure?

00:34:22.066 --> 00:34:25.400
I think again, the context is by allowing development within areas.

00:34:26.233 --> 00:34:28.100
I think they were characterizing it as areas

00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:31.400
where we project floodwaters to be.

00:34:31.934 --> 00:34:34.033
And the goal, it's not a singular goal.

00:34:34.066 --> 00:34:37.667
The plan outlines multiple goals, and what I think

00:34:37.734 --> 00:34:41.166
will be presented later in the presentation and was

00:34:41.266 --> 00:34:45.233
tried to be expressed within the plan is that there's multiple competing

00:34:45.266 --> 00:34:48.867
things that the community has to balance, and the policies in the plan try to

00:34:48.967 --> 00:34:50.900
strike a balance between those things.

00:34:50.934 --> 00:34:54.934
So yes, there is concerns around things like VOCs and

00:34:55.000 --> 00:34:56.567
the air emissions and the

00:34:57.400 --> 00:35:01.200
health conditions of the air, the floodwaters and where they're going, the traffic

00:35:01.300 --> 00:35:05.066
on Broadway, the urban design, the access to open space, the bike ped facilities,

00:35:06.133 --> 00:35:09.934
but there's also concerns around housing, fiscal revenues,

00:35:10.900 --> 00:35:14.767
creating community, creating access, creating open space without always

00:35:14.800 --> 00:35:17.567
doing it at the resident taxpayer's expense.

00:35:18.800 --> 00:35:21.300
And in trying to strike that balance, we're trying to hit on all of those goals.

00:35:21.367 --> 00:35:23.867
So there's economic development goals, there's housing goals, there's environmental

00:35:23.934 --> 00:35:26.800
goals, there's open space goals, there's remediation of brownfields goals.

00:35:27.567 --> 00:35:31.200
And what the committee has tried to strike is a balance of

00:35:31.266 --> 00:35:35.166
allowing some forms of development to try and achieve all of those goals

00:35:35.200 --> 00:35:38.300
but establish enough protections to avoid the risks.

00:35:39.066 --> 00:35:42.667
And then I'm not sure if this was framed as a question, but I did circle it.

00:35:43.133 --> 00:35:46.934
It was in the final comment there in reference to specifically recent

00:35:46.967 --> 00:35:50.867
legislation that was passed at the state level that forces communities

00:35:50.900 --> 00:35:52.033
to do certain things

00:35:52.900 --> 00:35:56.767
in some cases based on how we designate areas,

00:35:56.800 --> 00:35:59.166
whether they're growth or non-growth areas.

00:35:59.467 --> 00:36:02.066
And I just wanted to at least make the statement, and I'm happy to go into it

00:36:02.133 --> 00:36:05.967
deeper, is that this comprehensive plan fully responds to all of the

00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:09.200
current legislation and the legislation that we're aware of that hasn't been passed

00:36:09.700 --> 00:36:13.634
so that we're not at odds with any

00:36:13.667 --> 00:36:17.300
of that. And the growth designations that we have are not at odds with what the

00:36:17.400 --> 00:36:20.500
state has already expressed an interest in putting forward or what the state has

00:36:20.600 --> 00:36:21.300
already passed.

00:36:22.867 --> 00:36:26.767
I will also highlight that those changes from 2003, LD 2003 and

00:36:26.867 --> 00:36:27.967
LD 1829,

00:36:29.166 --> 00:36:30.800
the general

00:36:31.867 --> 00:36:35.000
description of those and their impacts in the development world is

00:36:35.400 --> 00:36:38.200
significantly larger than what the actual legislation does.

00:36:38.500 --> 00:36:42.500
For instance, LD 1829 is only active up to the first four units.

00:36:43.166 --> 00:36:47.100
It doesn't go beyond that. It doesn't enable indiscriminate development at 40 units

00:36:47.133 --> 00:36:48.400
per acre or something like that.

00:36:49.400 --> 00:36:53.066
So we've been tracking all of those bills and absorbed them into the plan, and the

00:36:53.100 --> 00:36:56.266
CPC, the Comprehensive Plan Committee, has reviewed what that

00:36:56.300 --> 00:36:58.800
legislation imposes and how to

00:36:58.834 --> 00:37:02.233
respond.Well, I'll leave it there if-

00:37:02.433 --> 00:37:03.834
There was a question about,

00:37:05.433 --> 00:37:09.133
I think this was related to if it's built, so if there's a new development,

00:37:09.200 --> 00:37:13.066
and I guess this could apply to existing development too, that becomes

00:37:13.200 --> 00:37:15.734
underwater. What does the city do then?

00:37:15.834 --> 00:37:19.600
I don't know if that's anything you can respond to in relation to the comp

00:37:19.634 --> 00:37:19.900
plan.

00:37:20.266 --> 00:37:20.533
Sure.

00:37:21.600 --> 00:37:25.133
And some of the context there, I think, was a citation from,

00:37:26.033 --> 00:37:29.166
I guess, some student mapping that was made available,

00:37:30.133 --> 00:37:33.900
referenced to 1.5 feet and 3 feet of sea level rise was

00:37:33.934 --> 00:37:37.700
that risk category. This plan requires us to prepare for at a

00:37:37.734 --> 00:37:41.166
minimum of 3.9 feet, so 1 foot above what

00:37:41.200 --> 00:37:44.767
was projected there, and up to 8.8 feet if we go

00:37:44.834 --> 00:37:48.400
to slightly larger scale developments or more critical infrastructure, things like

00:37:48.433 --> 00:37:50.066
city halls and whatnot.

00:37:51.233 --> 00:37:53.100
So we're preparing for significantly more.

00:37:53.133 --> 00:37:56.800
In fact, this plan would make South Portland the only community in the

00:37:56.834 --> 00:38:00.567
nation to actually try to prepare for an 8.8-foot scenario.

00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:03.700
No one else has done it or even come close to doing that.

00:38:04.400 --> 00:38:07.967
So the benchmark for what qualifies as a building that's

00:38:08.033 --> 00:38:11.934
capable of being there for the long term

00:38:12.066 --> 00:38:12.400
is

00:38:13.834 --> 00:38:17.567
a singular thing that only South Portland has defined as 8.8 feet.

00:38:17.834 --> 00:38:21.533
If it can't meet that threshold, it won't be a development that can

00:38:21.634 --> 00:38:25.233
proceed. So from the get-go, if a new building is proposed,

00:38:25.934 --> 00:38:29.567
it will certainly be able to weather those conditions or have to

00:38:29.600 --> 00:38:32.266
demonstrate that it can weather those conditions.

00:38:32.867 --> 00:38:36.634
There's also policy in the plan that says the council has zero

00:38:36.700 --> 00:38:40.567
obligation, and in fact, no expectation, which is breaking from the

00:38:40.567 --> 00:38:44.567
norm from decades ago, to accept any infrastructure that's

00:38:44.567 --> 00:38:48.433
proposed in areas that you deem are potential at-risk areas.

00:38:49.000 --> 00:38:52.900
So where, for instance, the Outer Highland Subdivisions, when

00:38:52.934 --> 00:38:55.934
they got built, a lot of those roads ended up turning into public roads.

00:38:56.000 --> 00:38:58.166
That's very common and very normal.

00:38:59.233 --> 00:39:02.266
Councils have always had the discretion to say, "No, thanks.

00:39:02.400 --> 00:39:05.166
We don't want that public park donated to us.

00:39:05.367 --> 00:39:07.133
Let it be private with public access.

00:39:07.567 --> 00:39:11.133
We don't want that road." "We don't want to own that sewer system." The Sable Oaks

00:39:11.266 --> 00:39:14.934
area, for instance, has a private sewer system. We never accepted it.

00:39:15.033 --> 00:39:18.533
City councils have always had that discretion, but they've never, or

00:39:18.734 --> 00:39:20.700
typically erred on the side of absorbing it.

00:39:20.700 --> 00:39:24.600
This plan says explicitly the council needs to do the due diligence of figuring

00:39:24.634 --> 00:39:28.367
out if any infrastructure should be absorbed as a public infrastructure.

00:39:28.367 --> 00:39:32.266
And if not, those remain the burden of the development to maintain and

00:39:32.433 --> 00:39:33.734
make sure that it's functional for

00:39:34.734 --> 00:39:38.367
that area. So we've tried to put in the checks and balances to make sure that the

00:39:38.367 --> 00:39:41.867
city is not paying for infrastructure it doesn't want to pay for, and that in the

00:39:41.900 --> 00:39:45.200
long term, it's not holding the bag for infrastructure

00:39:47.433 --> 00:39:49.433
that was serving a private development.

00:39:49.500 --> 00:39:52.000
Okay.

00:39:52.066 --> 00:39:52.667
That's all I have. Yep.

00:39:53.634 --> 00:39:55.033
All right. Thank you, Milan.

00:39:55.834 --> 00:39:57.867
And thank you to folks who asked questions.

00:39:57.967 --> 00:40:01.033
I feel like we've had a little bit of an appetizer for what might come

00:40:01.066 --> 00:40:05.033
later. We're moving to public hearings and action now.

00:40:05.266 --> 00:40:07.266
Madam City Clerk, could you read Ordinance

00:40:07.567 --> 00:40:09.433
2025-26?

00:40:11.233 --> 00:40:15.166
Ordinance number 2025-26, amending Chapter 4, Bicycles, of the Code of

00:40:15.233 --> 00:40:18.967
Ordinances to update the definition of a bicycle and add definition for the

00:40:19.033 --> 00:40:22.367
electric bicycle to better align with the state definition.

00:40:22.533 --> 00:40:25.967
Second reading. First reading was approved on April 7th, 2026.

00:40:26.367 --> 00:40:29.266
Passage will require a majority vote, and again, this will be a roll call vote.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.800
Thank you. Help me to remember that.

00:40:32.834 --> 00:40:35.333
Counselors, do you have questions on this item?

00:40:36.600 --> 00:40:38.533
I don't see any council questions.

00:40:39.734 --> 00:40:42.133
We can open this item up for public comment.

00:40:42.834 --> 00:40:46.667
Anyone have public comment on this item, please come to the microphone.

00:40:47.867 --> 00:40:49.467
Anyone? All right.

00:40:50.634 --> 00:40:53.066
We're going to close public comment on this item.

00:40:53.934 --> 00:40:54.567
And

00:40:55.667 --> 00:40:58.533
counselors, any discussion? I don't think so.

00:40:58.567 --> 00:41:02.367
It is a second read. So anyone? Anyone?

00:41:02.567 --> 00:41:03.767
We do have some discussion.

00:41:03.867 --> 00:41:04.533
Oh, no discussion.

00:41:04.567 --> 00:41:05.000
No, you're-

00:41:05.066 --> 00:41:05.667
Just move for passage of the second read

00:41:05.667 --> 00:41:08.867
... you're moving for passage. Okay. A second. Thank you.

00:41:08.967 --> 00:41:12.166
That was Counselor Walker moving, Counselor West seconding.

00:41:13.100 --> 00:41:14.533
Can we have our roll call vote?

00:41:15.967 --> 00:41:17.066
I'm going to ask for comments.

00:41:17.634 --> 00:41:18.767
Oh, do you have comments?

00:41:19.066 --> 00:41:22.433
I do. Just to say to some members of the community who have

00:41:22.634 --> 00:41:26.333
communicated with me on this, that what we're doing is bringing our

00:41:26.367 --> 00:41:29.767
definition of bicycle into conformance with state law.

00:41:30.367 --> 00:41:34.300
State law defines bicycle to include Class 1 and Class 2

00:41:34.333 --> 00:41:38.233
electric bikes. Therefore, if we allow bicycles on the green belt,

00:41:38.634 --> 00:41:42.233
it means we allow Class 1 and Class 2 electric bikes.

00:41:43.000 --> 00:41:44.734
It's not us doing anything different.

00:41:44.767 --> 00:41:47.533
It's just following state law.

00:41:48.400 --> 00:41:50.800
Thank you, Counselor West.

00:41:51.667 --> 00:41:53.300
All right. And you, no?

00:41:53.400 --> 00:41:53.700
Nothing to add.

00:41:53.734 --> 00:41:57.367
Counselor Walker? Okay. So now we're having our roll call vote.

00:41:58.133 --> 00:41:58.934
Counselor Matthews?

00:41:59.233 --> 00:41:59.667
Yes, ma'am.

00:41:59.967 --> 00:42:00.667
Counselor West?

00:42:01.233 --> 00:42:01.533
Yes.

00:42:01.834 --> 00:42:02.467
Counselor Pride?

00:42:02.867 --> 00:42:03.133
Yes.

00:42:04.133 --> 00:42:04.900
Counselor Scott?

00:42:06.300 --> 00:42:06.567
Yes.

00:42:07.200 --> 00:42:07.934
Counselor Walker?

00:42:08.233 --> 00:42:08.433
Yes.

00:42:08.767 --> 00:42:09.433
Counselor Coleman?

00:42:09.667 --> 00:42:09.934
Yes.

00:42:10.233 --> 00:42:10.900
And Mayor Tipton.

00:42:11.567 --> 00:42:12.433
Yes, thank you.

00:42:13.433 --> 00:42:16.734
All right. That ordinance passes unanimously. Thank you.

00:42:16.867 --> 00:42:19.533
Let's move to the next one, number 21.

00:42:20.200 --> 00:42:24.066
Ordinance number 2125-26, amending Chapter 15, Motor

00:42:24.133 --> 00:42:26.967
Vehicles and Traffic, of our Code of Ordinances to update the definition of

00:42:27.033 --> 00:42:29.133
bicycle. Again, this is a second read.

00:42:29.166 --> 00:42:31.934
The first reading passed on April 7th, 2026.

00:42:31.967 --> 00:42:34.567
This will require a majority vote, and again, will be a roll call vote.

00:42:35.533 --> 00:42:39.333
Thank you very much. Counselors, have questions developed since our first reading?

00:42:39.533 --> 00:42:39.767
Mm-mm.

00:42:41.033 --> 00:42:44.233
I don't see questions. Do we have public comment on this item?

00:42:44.667 --> 00:42:46.166
Ordinance 21.

00:42:47.634 --> 00:42:47.934
Don't-

00:42:49.100 --> 00:42:53.033
Does that include speed regulations, since electric bikes is

00:42:53.066 --> 00:42:53.900
normally traveling faster?

00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:54.300
All right.

00:42:56.133 --> 00:42:59.934
Okay. To refresh my

00:42:59.967 --> 00:43:01.133
memory, what's your name again?

00:43:01.233 --> 00:43:01.767
Edward Reiner.

00:43:02.533 --> 00:43:03.033
Okay.

00:43:03.634 --> 00:43:04.100
Reiner.

00:43:05.333 --> 00:43:07.867
We prefer you come to the microphone if that works for you.

00:43:07.967 --> 00:43:09.266
Let me know if it doesn't.

00:43:09.333 --> 00:43:09.634
Yes.

00:43:10.533 --> 00:43:11.266
If you want a full comment.

00:43:11.467 --> 00:43:13.767
Do we have an answer to the question?

00:43:14.367 --> 00:43:18.066
There is no, in this ordinance, there is no cap on

00:43:18.166 --> 00:43:22.000
speeds. Class one and two do have governors on them, so they can only reach certain

00:43:22.066 --> 00:43:25.333
speeds. Class three can reach higher, but those are not allowed.

00:43:26.100 --> 00:43:28.667
We did do a speed

00:43:29.700 --> 00:43:32.133
study that was talked about during the first

00:43:33.634 --> 00:43:37.000
discussion of this, and

00:43:37.467 --> 00:43:41.066
there, generally speaking, wasn't that vast of a difference between what they

00:43:41.133 --> 00:43:44.533
measured as what they could perceive the e-bikes were, because sometimes it's hard

00:43:44.567 --> 00:43:47.367
to tell. But our parks staff had a hard time discerning.

00:43:48.000 --> 00:43:51.834
But the ones they could discern, it was maybe a couple miles per

00:43:51.900 --> 00:43:52.667
hour difference.

00:43:53.000 --> 00:43:53.467
Right. So,

00:43:54.567 --> 00:43:56.433
my name is Edward Reiner, 25 Ballinger.

00:43:56.767 --> 00:43:59.967
So, I'm on the Greenbelt Trail with my bicycle a lot,

00:44:00.066 --> 00:44:03.667
and what we've noticed, and this is true of any traffic pattern,

00:44:03.767 --> 00:44:04.700
if

00:44:05.533 --> 00:44:09.233
one vehicle, one bicycle is traveling significantly

00:44:09.266 --> 00:44:12.233
faster, it's dangerous for bicyclists and

00:44:13.166 --> 00:44:16.233
pedestrians because they're not used to

00:44:16.300 --> 00:44:20.133
that approach or someone coming from behind that fast.

00:44:20.166 --> 00:44:23.634
So, I'm trying to be proactive and think that also that the

00:44:23.834 --> 00:44:25.767
class three very speedy

00:44:27.333 --> 00:44:31.100
electric bikes may be ending up on the trail, whether they're

00:44:31.166 --> 00:44:34.900
allowed or not. So, I'm thinking there should be some type of...

00:44:36.600 --> 00:44:37.667
So it's on the books that

00:44:39.266 --> 00:44:41.166
there is such a concept as speeding,

00:44:42.467 --> 00:44:44.967
which would cover the discrepancy

00:44:45.066 --> 00:44:48.567
between fast bicycles, people who are

00:44:48.767 --> 00:44:52.367
bicycle athletes, and people who are going faster than that

00:44:53.133 --> 00:44:55.967
on electric bikes. So there is a difference, I think,

00:44:56.033 --> 00:44:59.266
between the strongest cyclists and people

00:45:00.433 --> 00:45:00.934
on fast

00:45:02.033 --> 00:45:06.000
electric bikes. So, my comments were just to see

00:45:06.033 --> 00:45:09.567
if we could do something proactively rather than having to respond to

00:45:09.634 --> 00:45:10.367
violations

00:45:11.233 --> 00:45:13.100
or safety concerns.

00:45:14.133 --> 00:45:14.467
Thank you.

00:45:15.333 --> 00:45:18.834
Thank you very much. Did you want to quickly address,

00:45:20.033 --> 00:45:23.266
would that be a workshop item or that was actually a question.

00:45:23.500 --> 00:45:26.033
Can we proactively address this?

00:45:26.767 --> 00:45:29.467
You could add in, if you wanted to add in speed limits.

00:45:30.367 --> 00:45:34.333
It all goes back to the same thing that we've talked about before, the enforcement.

00:45:35.767 --> 00:45:38.433
Right now, as you know, there's e-bikes on the Greenbelt even though they're

00:45:38.467 --> 00:45:42.400
technically not allowed, and we don't really have much by the

00:45:42.433 --> 00:45:45.834
way of proactive enforcement. So, we do generally have to respond

00:45:45.867 --> 00:45:49.800
to complaints if we get them, so it would be the same thing

00:45:49.867 --> 00:45:53.166
with speed enforcement. We don't have a dedicated person that's going to be able to

00:45:53.166 --> 00:45:56.667
sit there with a speed gun. But understanding that,

00:45:57.033 --> 00:46:00.934
even so, you could still put in speed restrictions.

00:46:01.667 --> 00:46:05.266
