04:10:57.400 --> 04:11:01.266
I wanted to provide a few brief comments, and please let

04:11:01.333 --> 04:11:04.934
me know if this glitches out. I first wanted to

04:11:05.000 --> 04:11:08.967
speak to the way that we are speaking to each other, and I have been disheartened

04:11:09.000 --> 04:11:12.767
to hear in many different scenarios and discussions in

04:11:12.800 --> 04:11:16.600
South Portland that we have, I think, felt

04:11:16.767 --> 04:11:20.333
disrespected or dismissed. And I have seen this on all sides

04:11:20.367 --> 04:11:24.300
of the discussion. So, this is not to any one group

04:11:24.367 --> 04:11:27.934
or one side of any of these arguments, but I hope that we can speak to each other

04:11:27.967 --> 04:11:29.433
with respect and

04:11:31.133 --> 04:11:35.033
again, all sides going forward, and make sure that we are open to

04:11:35.133 --> 04:11:38.333
communication and hearing everyone's arguments.

04:11:39.266 --> 04:11:40.967
So just wanted to put that out there.

04:11:41.734 --> 04:11:44.934
I think with regard to the comprehensive plan, thank you so much for all of the

04:11:44.934 --> 04:11:48.900
work that has gone into this, all of the public commentary, and the hours

04:11:48.967 --> 04:11:51.800
and hours that have been spent on this plan.

04:11:52.166 --> 04:11:56.133
I am in support of moving the plan as is forward, and am happy to hear

04:11:56.166 --> 04:11:56.300
and

04:11:57.133 --> 04:11:58.767
decide on motions as we get there.

04:12:00.066 --> 04:12:03.433
I want everyone to know that air quality and toxic

04:12:04.700 --> 04:12:08.600
fumes are incredibly important to me, and I do believe that

04:12:08.634 --> 04:12:12.100
we have a lot of work to do as a city to continue in this effort.

04:12:12.266 --> 04:12:15.767
I just don't believe that the level of specificity that has been

04:12:15.767 --> 04:12:19.266
requested is appropriate for a comprehensive plan.

04:12:19.800 --> 04:12:23.500
I believe very strongly that we need to be planning for and

04:12:23.800 --> 04:12:27.367
appreciative of climate change, and I think that the climate resiliency

04:12:27.467 --> 04:12:31.233
overlay zone is an incredibly progressive and forward-looking

04:12:31.400 --> 04:12:35.367
step to move in that direction. I know that there is

04:12:35.400 --> 04:12:38.934
great concern about soil contamination, and I believe strongly that

04:12:39.000 --> 04:12:42.200
we do have the technology... Oops, let me make sure I'm

04:12:42.300 --> 04:12:43.400
not... Nope.

04:12:45.767 --> 04:12:46.667
Did you lose me again?

04:12:46.900 --> 04:12:47.333
We're still here.

04:12:47.500 --> 04:12:48.066
Keep going, good.

04:12:48.100 --> 04:12:48.500
We're here.

04:12:48.667 --> 04:12:50.400
Okay, great.

04:12:51.233 --> 04:12:54.867
I believe that we have the ability to remediate that, and if we give up on

04:12:54.900 --> 04:12:57.233
areas of our world that have been

04:12:59.066 --> 04:13:03.033
challenged by environmental concerns in the past, then we really have given

04:13:03.133 --> 04:13:04.233
up on too much.

04:13:05.533 --> 04:13:09.467
There were many comments and many requests for different areas of the plan

04:13:09.500 --> 04:13:13.467
to be amended, and many of them, I think, are just far too

04:13:13.634 --> 04:13:16.700
specific and not appropriate for a comprehensive plan.

04:13:17.533 --> 04:13:18.800
Thousand-foot buffers,

04:13:19.634 --> 04:13:22.934
specific modeling requests, there's many out there.

04:13:23.100 --> 04:13:26.834
I just don't think that that is appropriate for a comprehensive

04:13:26.934 --> 04:13:27.233
plan.

04:13:28.500 --> 04:13:31.767
Regarding the Save Our Shipyard and expanding the Bug Light Park,

04:13:32.200 --> 04:13:34.166
obviously, this is near and dear to all of us.

04:13:34.266 --> 04:13:38.033
I don't think there was anyone that would not be in

04:13:38.066 --> 04:13:41.667
favor of expanding Bug Light Park, both to the south with the

04:13:41.734 --> 04:13:44.066
PPL properties and elsewhere across the city.

04:13:45.033 --> 04:13:48.667
So I want those members to know that I am

04:13:49.467 --> 04:13:53.300
in favor of this. I'd love to sit down with more of you and

04:13:53.333 --> 04:13:57.300
talk about this and see about ways that the city can partner with your

04:13:57.333 --> 04:14:01.100
organization, with other organizations, with private landowners, to

04:14:01.133 --> 04:14:04.800
expand Bug Light Park and to make part of this vision happen.

04:14:04.967 --> 04:14:08.734
I think it is very inappropriate to do that through a comprehensive plan and

04:14:08.867 --> 04:14:10.266
zoning, and I think

04:14:12.066 --> 04:14:15.900
I can go on and on about this, and I'm happy to have more conversations, but I just

04:14:15.934 --> 04:14:18.867
don't believe that that's the correct way or the legal way to

04:14:20.433 --> 04:14:23.467
go about this. So happy to continue to have that conversation.

04:14:23.533 --> 04:14:27.500
I've started some of those conversations, but please know that my support is there

04:14:28.266 --> 04:14:31.734
for Bug Light. I think the last thing that I would say

04:14:32.734 --> 04:14:36.467
is in thinking about whether or not we send this plan

04:14:36.767 --> 04:14:40.567
back, I've heard lots of commentary, both at the

04:14:40.634 --> 04:14:44.367
comprehensive planning meetings, in emails, in discussions with people.

04:14:44.467 --> 04:14:48.033
If I were to send this plan back to the comprehensive plan or put a

04:14:48.066 --> 04:14:51.867
motion forward, it would actually be to remove the lines and remove the

04:14:51.934 --> 04:14:55.567
specificity in the Eastern Waterfront and allow for the

04:14:55.634 --> 04:14:58.900
zoning process and the specifics to play out.

04:14:59.367 --> 04:14:59.867
Lost it.

04:15:00.100 --> 04:15:03.100
All right, just a little bit. It would be to remove...

04:15:05.133 --> 04:15:08.567
I don't believe the specificity, the

04:15:08.634 --> 04:15:10.266
lines, the heights,

04:15:11.166 --> 04:15:14.700
the commentary in the Eastern Waterfront is

04:15:14.767 --> 04:15:18.300
appropriate. I appreciate that it was done and I'm willing to accept it, but

04:15:18.367 --> 04:15:19.500
that would be

04:15:20.700 --> 04:15:22.934
the amendment that I would request.

04:15:23.467 --> 04:15:27.033
So that's sort of my compromise, just going forward knowing that.

04:15:27.367 --> 04:15:30.967
I believe this area is severely down zoned, and I'm very

04:15:31.066 --> 04:15:35.033
concerned that we keep pushing in that direction, that we're going down

04:15:35.066 --> 04:15:38.800
a bad path.Again, happy to discuss all of

04:15:38.900 --> 04:15:42.800
this. I think the last thing that I will say, and this is not

04:15:42.834 --> 04:15:46.734
necessarily part of the comprehensive plan, but hearing the

04:15:46.734 --> 04:15:50.266
discussion and the arguments, I hear so many

04:15:50.367 --> 04:15:53.934
comments that say, "I want to live here, and I don't want

04:15:54.033 --> 04:15:57.934
anyone else, any more people to live here." And that is

04:15:58.033 --> 04:16:01.433
a statement that says, "I belong here, and you don't."

04:16:02.100 --> 04:16:03.934
And I can't tell you how

04:16:05.400 --> 04:16:09.100
sad and disappointed and angry that makes me feel,

04:16:09.867 --> 04:16:13.634
because when I moved to this town, I wanted to belong, and I wanted to be

04:16:13.734 --> 04:16:17.433
welcomed. And I hope that new residents who come, people who

04:16:17.500 --> 04:16:21.266
want to move into South Portland, feel welcomed, and that we are able

04:16:21.367 --> 04:16:25.300
to create and enable a space for them to be and for them

04:16:25.333 --> 04:16:29.000
to belong. So, I appreciate all of the arguments

04:16:29.033 --> 04:16:31.467
about air quality, climate change,

04:16:32.300 --> 04:16:36.066
all of those. I don't appreciate the arguments about we don't want any more

04:16:36.133 --> 04:16:39.800
people in our town. So, I would just encourage people, as you think

04:16:39.934 --> 04:16:43.467
about everything that you do in this space, what is your

04:16:43.533 --> 04:16:45.133
privilege to be here? How

04:16:45.967 --> 04:16:48.433
are you presenting yourself? How do you welcome others?

04:16:48.567 --> 04:16:52.200
Are you being inclusive, or are you not being

04:16:52.233 --> 04:16:56.133
inclusive? And I think if we take some of that away, and we sort

04:16:56.166 --> 04:17:00.066
of spend a little time processing and unpacking some of those

04:17:00.100 --> 04:17:04.033
emotions, I hope that we can come forward with South Portland and

04:17:04.100 --> 04:17:07.900
welcome new people and build the housing that we need, and

04:17:07.900 --> 04:17:11.634
build back our school populations and really have the

04:17:11.667 --> 04:17:14.634
wonderful community that I think we all love and hold dear.

04:17:14.900 --> 04:17:17.500
So, that's my last comment. I'm supportive of this plan.

04:17:17.533 --> 04:17:21.500
I hope we can move it forward. And I'm really excited to get into the details

04:17:21.567 --> 04:17:25.433
of the actual implementation and getting some of this policy work

04:17:25.467 --> 04:17:26.834
done. Thank you.

04:17:28.800 --> 04:17:32.734
Thank you very much, Carter. You came in loud and clear at last, and

04:17:32.767 --> 04:17:35.300
we're happy to have heard your comment. Thank you.

04:17:38.033 --> 04:17:38.367
All right.

04:17:40.433 --> 04:17:40.734
Yes?

04:17:41.367 --> 04:17:45.000
I just figured while people are considering more amendments, I can filibuster a

04:17:45.000 --> 04:17:46.333
little more because I have none to offer.

04:17:47.200 --> 04:17:50.867
But I would like to address the comprehensive plan.

04:17:52.033 --> 04:17:52.467
And

04:17:53.400 --> 04:17:56.333
I, like Carter, would move it forward as written.

04:17:57.033 --> 04:17:58.867
I want to support her

04:18:01.000 --> 04:18:01.600
in that

04:18:02.467 --> 04:18:04.867
all of you probably didn't see all the emails we did .

04:18:05.634 --> 04:18:09.100
And there were many people who emailed us saying things that had the

04:18:10.900 --> 04:18:11.500
air of,

04:18:12.467 --> 04:18:16.300
"We live here. We don't want anybody else to live here," and that kind of stuff.

04:18:16.367 --> 04:18:20.233
There were people who emailed us who said that, and that tone was not appreciated.

04:18:20.266 --> 04:18:21.834
And so I can understand where she's coming from.

04:18:22.433 --> 04:18:26.033
She was speaking to the wider audience, not necessarily the people in the room.

04:18:26.300 --> 04:18:29.767
So I just wanted to clarify, at least I don't want to ascribe her motives, but I

04:18:29.800 --> 04:18:33.266
believe that to be true, because I don't feel like we heard that much from you all

04:18:33.266 --> 04:18:37.266
tonight. You all had similar concerns to ones I've always had as a councilor.

04:18:38.433 --> 04:18:42.166
I am for open space. I supported the piggery being purchased by the--

04:18:43.333 --> 04:18:47.133
I supported the open space bond. I supported this new property that we

04:18:47.166 --> 04:18:50.800
have by Pilgrim Road, and having that remain

04:18:50.900 --> 04:18:54.667
conservation space. I've been repeatedly

04:18:56.433 --> 04:18:57.133
someone who's very

04:18:58.133 --> 04:19:00.967
much in favor of environmentalism in the city, sustainability.

04:19:01.767 --> 04:19:05.734
I started getting involved in city politics when they were suggesting that we have

04:19:05.800 --> 04:19:09.734
propane unloading in the railroad yard, and I was really

04:19:09.734 --> 04:19:13.667
against that, and it was one of the things that influenced me to

04:19:13.734 --> 04:19:16.300
get involved and eventually run for council.

04:19:17.100 --> 04:19:19.433
And I supported the continuation of the lawsuit

04:19:19.634 --> 04:19:23.600
against the Clear Skies Ordinance that we eventually won

04:19:23.634 --> 04:19:27.333
while I was mayor of the city. I was proud of what we did as a

04:19:27.400 --> 04:19:27.834
community.

04:19:29.667 --> 04:19:33.567
As part of that, I testified to the legislature supporting fence line

04:19:33.634 --> 04:19:37.433
monitoring, and I think that support helped get us that law

04:19:37.634 --> 04:19:39.667
in place, and I'm proud of that.

04:19:41.734 --> 04:19:44.166
I was a key vote in getting the tree ordinance passed.

04:19:45.266 --> 04:19:47.533
I'm the one who tried to get the

04:19:49.567 --> 04:19:53.367
leaf blower ordinance passed and had my life threatened for it, which is a

04:19:53.433 --> 04:19:57.233
little crazy still to say that out loud, but it happened, and we ended up

04:19:57.300 --> 04:20:01.266
sort of dropping that. And part of me still feels we need to get rid of

04:20:01.300 --> 04:20:04.333
two-stroke engines in general because they are just horrible emissions

04:20:05.867 --> 04:20:08.567
producers and horrible for the person operating it.

04:20:08.567 --> 04:20:10.667
But that's not what we're talking about tonight.

04:20:10.867 --> 04:20:13.900
Tonight, we're talking about the comprehensive plan.

04:20:13.967 --> 04:20:17.900
And if we look where we were in 2012 when we passed the

04:20:17.967 --> 04:20:21.800
comprehensive plan, we will see why city staff

04:20:21.900 --> 04:20:25.834
talked to the Packards and talked to them about developing that land the way

04:20:25.900 --> 04:20:29.500
they did. Because it specifically says in that comprehensive plan

04:20:29.967 --> 04:20:33.634
that city staff, city basic policy is to

04:20:33.634 --> 04:20:35.800
encourage good quality development in this area.

04:20:35.934 --> 04:20:39.900
To accomplish this objective, the city should actively work with property

04:20:39.934 --> 04:20:43.467
owners. And it doesn't specify no residential.

04:20:44.066 --> 04:20:44.266
Now,

04:20:45.500 --> 04:20:48.800
they asked for a zone change, and in fact, our planning board

04:20:49.266 --> 04:20:52.767
said, "Yeah, that fits with the comprehensive plan because staff is supposed to

04:20:52.800 --> 04:20:55.567
work with them," and it doesn't say anything about it not being

04:20:55.634 --> 04:20:59.367
residential. And what ended up happening, I think, and I

04:20:59.433 --> 04:20:59.900
can't say this

04:21:01.033 --> 04:21:04.967
with complete clarity because they withdrew their application, but I think

04:21:05.000 --> 04:21:08.867
they spoke to some councilors, and including myself, because I know they

04:21:08.867 --> 04:21:12.767
did, because I spoke to them. And I made my opinion public, which was

04:21:12.800 --> 04:21:15.800
that I don't think the people who bought near the

04:21:16.300 --> 04:21:20.033
shipyard, who bought near that zone of what it's

04:21:20.066 --> 04:21:23.467
zoned as now, working waterfront, thought that there would be a

04:21:23.467 --> 04:21:27.233
development. And the people who bought near it get to rely on that

04:21:27.333 --> 04:21:27.734
zoning.

04:21:28.800 --> 04:21:29.867
That's just my opinion.

04:21:30.800 --> 04:21:34.500
Now we're talking about a comprehensive plan that doesn't

04:21:34.533 --> 04:21:36.233
necessarily say there's going to be

04:21:38.567 --> 04:21:42.367
residential. It says they have to meet certain requirements that we get to set.

04:21:42.467 --> 04:21:45.066
That was one of the purposes of my question early on to Milan

04:21:45.166 --> 04:21:49.066
about who gets to decide how

04:21:49.100 --> 04:21:50.400
the health of the

04:21:51.367 --> 04:21:54.634
people living nearby the tanks is assessed. We do.

04:21:54.667 --> 04:21:56.767
We could set a really, really high bar.

04:21:56.834 --> 04:22:00.800
If you guys continue to support councilors who are

04:22:00.834 --> 04:22:04.066
environmentally minded, we can set a really high bar for

04:22:05.867 --> 04:22:09.367
developers to meet before we allow residential, and they may never be able to meet

04:22:09.400 --> 04:22:13.000
it because we can set the bar that high. It's allowed.

04:22:15.000 --> 04:22:15.233
So

04:22:16.233 --> 04:22:17.900
I think it's interesting because I

04:22:19.166 --> 04:22:23.000
live right up the hill here. So every morning, I pull out of my

04:22:23.066 --> 04:22:27.066
driveway, and I see the Hill Street tank farm, every morning.

04:22:27.867 --> 04:22:31.567
And if you look at another Nutter Hill neighborhood, the K

04:22:31.567 --> 04:22:35.266
Lupa 16, which has been applauded by people, including Toss the

04:22:35.333 --> 04:22:39.200
Tanks folks, who obviously have an environmental bent to

04:22:39.266 --> 04:22:42.734
them, but if you look at that K Lupa, it

04:22:44.734 --> 04:22:48.734
says, "Amends zoning to primarily encourage the development of complete

04:22:48.767 --> 04:22:52.734
neighborhood, mixed residential, and light commercial." So in this

04:22:52.800 --> 04:22:56.166
area, we are promoting light residential,

04:22:56.934 --> 04:22:57.133
and

04:22:58.367 --> 04:23:02.200
that's right near the tanks. And I just don't hear folks saying, "Well, how can we

04:23:02.266 --> 04:23:04.200
allow light residential near the tanks?"

04:23:06.567 --> 04:23:09.033
They're not all in use, and I

04:23:10.367 --> 04:23:12.066
haven't seen the fence line data there.

04:23:12.400 --> 04:23:14.467
In fact, I think maybe one or two of them are in use.

04:23:14.567 --> 04:23:16.467
But if they suddenly all were put into action,

04:23:17.333 --> 04:23:19.300
I think I'd be in trouble, and I live uphill,

04:23:20.667 --> 04:23:24.533
potentially. Maybe the downhill is good for me, but it's not good for Kaylor

04:23:24.600 --> 04:23:25.667
School while it's still

04:23:26.533 --> 04:23:27.867
open, I guess.

04:23:28.700 --> 04:23:31.934
But all that being said, you look at that

04:23:32.800 --> 04:23:36.200
K Lupa 16 language is very much okay with

04:23:36.300 --> 04:23:39.500
residential. If you compare that to the language in

04:23:39.667 --> 04:23:43.533
22 about residential, where it says residential should only be

04:23:43.600 --> 04:23:47.533
permitted if they meet this burden of having a health assessment.

04:23:48.100 --> 04:23:52.000
That's very different language. And again, it's policy

04:23:52.066 --> 04:23:55.934
guidance, right? We have the 2012 comp plan says the city

04:23:55.967 --> 04:23:59.800
should work with a developer to get as

04:23:59.834 --> 04:24:03.400
much suitable development that matches the neighborhood, which would include

04:24:03.467 --> 04:24:06.900
residential, as possible. And yet, that didn't happen because the

04:24:06.900 --> 04:24:10.700
zoning is what I think defined it in most councilors' minds

04:24:11.066 --> 04:24:14.734
what should go there. And I think that's why the Packards

04:24:14.767 --> 04:24:17.467
withdrew, because they talked to me and some other councilors who all said, "Well,

04:24:17.533 --> 04:24:20.567
it's not really zoned for you. You should've thought about the zoning when you

04:24:20.600 --> 04:24:21.000
bought it."

04:24:22.634 --> 04:24:25.200
It's the zoning that's really going to offer that granularity,

04:24:26.800 --> 04:24:30.767
and that's why I support the plan as is because I think it supports zoning

04:24:31.266 --> 04:24:35.233
that is restrictive, that will make it so housing is difficult to go

04:24:35.300 --> 04:24:36.100
there because

04:24:37.100 --> 04:24:41.066
we, the decision-makers, are people, I think, who will support that

04:24:41.100 --> 04:24:43.967
higher standard in zoning. That being said,

04:24:44.700 --> 04:24:45.800
I went

04:24:47.000 --> 04:24:50.300
to Josh Cutler's house, and I saw the presentation on the park, and that does

04:24:50.367 --> 04:24:54.133
excite me. I would totally support that. We don't own the land.

04:24:54.367 --> 04:24:58.200
That's my one thing. And we, and the school, we're all

04:24:58.300 --> 04:25:00.367
in a big fiscal,

04:25:01.333 --> 04:25:02.834
kind of looking at a fiscal cliff here.

04:25:03.700 --> 04:25:06.567
And so us buying the land is almost an impossibility.

04:25:07.867 --> 04:25:11.166
I know that the Packards bought it, what, 7.7 million in 2018.

04:25:12.133 --> 04:25:13.033
Even without

04:25:14.600 --> 04:25:17.200
us talking about it, the land has gone up in value.

04:25:17.233 --> 04:25:20.967
And people tell me that if the city says they're interested in a parcel, it

04:25:21.000 --> 04:25:21.667
doubles in value,

04:25:23.200 --> 04:25:26.967
just automatically. If the city's going for it because the people who own land

04:25:27.100 --> 04:25:30.400
think the city's pockets are as deep as they need to be because of bonding and

04:25:30.433 --> 04:25:32.066
whatnot. So I

04:25:33.066 --> 04:25:35.800
am totally for it. Just like Carter, I would support it

04:25:36.667 --> 04:25:40.200
wholeheartedly. I'm happy to continue that conversation and see what

04:25:40.700 --> 04:25:43.266
things we can do to make that a reality.

04:25:43.867 --> 04:25:47.500
I just agree that I don't really think it fits in a comp plan.

04:25:47.700 --> 04:25:50.834
I think zoning, but zoning's only going to happen if someone else owns that

04:25:50.867 --> 04:25:53.967
property because we can't zone someone out of their

04:25:54.967 --> 04:25:57.367
property. That just would be illegal.

04:25:57.433 --> 04:26:00.634
So that's where I'm at, and I hope that gave people time

04:26:00.667 --> 04:26:04.667
to think. But as I said, I support this comp

04:26:04.667 --> 04:26:08.333
plan as is, as amended, and I also consider other amendments.

04:26:08.667 --> 04:26:12.533
Just because other people amend it certain ways doesn't mean that I won't be for

04:26:12.567 --> 04:26:13.734
it after those amendments.

04:26:15.567 --> 04:26:17.400
Well, then try this one.

04:26:18.066 --> 04:26:18.734
You're ready then?

04:26:19.300 --> 04:26:19.367
Yes.

04:26:19.367 --> 04:26:21.033
I filibustered enough for you, Mayor?

04:26:21.400 --> 04:26:21.734
Yes.

04:26:21.767 --> 04:26:22.500
Good.

04:26:22.734 --> 04:26:24.266
I really did try. I have some

04:26:25.600 --> 04:26:29.400
confusion about what you said, but I followed most of it, I

04:26:29.500 --> 04:26:33.166
believe. Okay, never mind. Can I just ask you, Councilor

04:26:33.266 --> 04:26:33.500
Pride,

04:26:34.600 --> 04:26:38.333
toward the end, it sounded like you were saying

04:26:38.367 --> 04:26:38.600
that

04:26:40.100 --> 04:26:43.333
you're concerned that... We are basically talking about

04:26:43.400 --> 04:26:44.333
upzoning.

04:26:46.767 --> 04:26:46.867
No.

04:26:47.200 --> 04:26:47.767
What is that?

04:26:49.000 --> 04:26:52.967
To make land more valuable because of what it can be

04:26:53.100 --> 04:26:53.767
used for.

04:26:55.000 --> 04:26:55.166
So I don't-

04:26:55.200 --> 04:26:56.400
Well, the old plan does that,

04:26:57.200 --> 04:27:01.166
and what we're saying is now we're actually restricting it from being

04:27:01.166 --> 04:27:03.734
residential unless they jump through a bunch of hoops.

04:27:03.800 --> 04:27:06.400
But where in the old plan did it zone it residential?

04:27:06.567 --> 04:27:10.166
It said that the staff should work with them to develop whatever they want.

04:27:10.500 --> 04:27:13.333
We should put the land to the most valuable use possible, basically.

04:27:13.367 --> 04:27:15.333
We'll have to agree to dance on

04:27:16.467 --> 04:27:17.367
this pin top.

04:27:17.467 --> 04:27:20.900
It wasn't specific, but it does not restrict it at all.

04:27:21.033 --> 04:27:21.033
It says staff should work with-

04:27:21.066 --> 04:27:23.133
All right. Well, I see your hand, Councilor Russ.

04:27:23.200 --> 04:27:25.967
I was going to offer the motion, but would you like to speak?

04:27:26.300 --> 04:27:29.967
Well, I'd just like to point, the land right now, the comprehensive

04:27:30.033 --> 04:27:33.934
plan, the 2012 comprehensive plan specifically says mixed use,

04:27:34.333 --> 04:27:37.166
and the existing zoning is 86 feet

04:27:37.800 --> 04:27:41.567
So, the proposed plan is a significant down

04:27:41.634 --> 04:27:41.900
zone

04:27:42.500 --> 04:27:45.166
Yes, in the height things, absolutely. Yeah. Yes.

04:27:46.066 --> 04:27:48.667
But it never said residential, and now it will.

04:27:48.767 --> 04:27:50.667
So anyway, unless-

04:27:50.734 --> 04:27:51.800
But only if they meet the-

04:27:51.867 --> 04:27:52.700
No, sorry.

04:27:55.000 --> 04:27:56.300
It doesn't say residential, per se.

04:27:56.300 --> 04:27:56.867
No, it doesn't.

04:27:56.900 --> 04:27:58.266
All right. I will just-

04:27:58.367 --> 04:27:58.834
No, it doesn't. It makes two years of difference

04:27:58.834 --> 04:28:00.266
... offer this.

04:28:00.467 --> 04:28:00.467
Right.

04:28:00.533 --> 04:28:01.600
It does.

04:28:01.667 --> 04:28:05.567
I move to amend the shipyard district language,

04:28:05.667 --> 04:28:09.166
the land use language, to add the following, "Residential and

04:28:09.200 --> 04:28:12.934
lodging uses within the shipyard district shall not be permitted

04:28:12.967 --> 04:28:16.266
unless petroleum storage and transfer operations have been

04:28:16.333 --> 04:28:18.734
permanently discontinued."

04:28:21.066 --> 04:28:22.166
Do we have a second?

04:28:23.767 --> 04:28:25.967
Could you repeat that?

04:28:26.100 --> 04:28:30.066
Hold it. Residential and lodging uses within the shipyard district shall

04:28:30.100 --> 04:28:30.967
not be permitted

04:28:32.500 --> 04:28:35.834
unless petroleum storage and transfer operations have been

04:28:35.900 --> 04:28:37.533
permanently discontinued.

04:28:42.634 --> 04:28:46.333
That kind of precludes 21, which you said

04:28:46.400 --> 04:28:49.367
was the best place for a park along the Fore River.

04:28:50.100 --> 04:28:51.266
Thank you-

04:28:51.400 --> 04:28:51.433
Excludes, not precludes

04:28:51.433 --> 04:28:54.233
... Councilor Coleman, but I think what I need is a second-

04:28:54.767 --> 04:28:55.667
No... or no second.

04:28:56.700 --> 04:28:58.967
So, so far I don't see a second,

04:28:59.867 --> 04:29:01.767
and you're not seconding it either. All right.

04:29:02.066 --> 04:29:04.367
So that motion doesn't even become a motion.

04:29:05.467 --> 04:29:09.400
Let's try another one, if you would just hear me on this one.

04:29:11.500 --> 04:29:15.300
This is with the Section 5C13 language,

04:29:15.467 --> 04:29:19.300
and it is not highly specific, but what I

04:29:19.367 --> 04:29:22.100
would add to the language is,

04:29:23.967 --> 04:29:27.567
"The city shall incorporate air dispersion and

04:29:27.767 --> 04:29:31.500
human exposure modeling using best available science

04:29:31.600 --> 04:29:34.900
and data reflective of full

04:29:35.100 --> 04:29:39.000
permitted or licensed operational capacity

04:29:39.066 --> 04:29:42.734
to inform land use decisions, public health assessments, and

04:29:42.900 --> 04:29:46.734
future policy development in areas

04:29:46.867 --> 04:29:50.800
proximate to petroleum storage and transfer facilities."

04:29:53.266 --> 04:29:53.734
I think you're going to have to read that again.

04:29:53.734 --> 04:29:55.500
It's not asking for a specific one.

04:29:55.533 --> 04:29:55.533
Yeah.

04:29:55.567 --> 04:29:56.700
It is suggesting that

04:29:57.967 --> 04:29:58.500
as we...

04:29:59.600 --> 04:30:02.000
Well, first of all, I don't see a second, so I don't think it's-

04:30:02.066 --> 04:30:02.967
Oh, I might. I just need-

04:30:03.000 --> 04:30:03.066
You might

04:30:03.166 --> 04:30:03.867
... to hear it again.

04:30:03.967 --> 04:30:07.533
All right. So we've put in there some

04:30:07.600 --> 04:30:10.934
language that says some health

04:30:11.400 --> 04:30:15.100
standards must be met. My concern

04:30:15.166 --> 04:30:18.266
has always been that

04:30:19.367 --> 04:30:23.266
health standards can kind of change depending on what state

04:30:23.333 --> 04:30:27.300
you're standing in, depending on what administration you might

04:30:27.400 --> 04:30:31.100
have at the state or federal level, depending on whether your lawyer is

04:30:31.166 --> 04:30:32.767
better than the other person's lawyer.

04:30:32.800 --> 04:30:32.867
So,

04:30:33.800 --> 04:30:37.734
with the modeling idea, I think it takes a lot of the data,

04:30:37.867 --> 04:30:41.500
and like the weather is forecasted, it

04:30:41.567 --> 04:30:43.433
forecasts where

04:30:44.266 --> 04:30:48.200
the emissions are going. And I did hear earlier

04:30:48.233 --> 04:30:50.300
in this discussion, I'm losing track of who said it, but it

04:30:52.200 --> 04:30:55.767
might have even been a staff member. I don't know. No, maybe it was you.

04:30:56.100 --> 04:30:59.033
It was Scott. Scott. You talked about

04:30:59.900 --> 04:31:03.767
knowing more about dispersion and where it's ending up,

04:31:04.066 --> 04:31:06.467
and that's what modeling would help us do. Yes.

04:31:06.567 --> 04:31:08.500
I just needed you to reread the language.

04:31:08.667 --> 04:31:09.700
Oh, you didn't need a speech?

04:31:09.934 --> 04:31:09.934
No.

04:31:09.967 --> 04:31:12.333
God darn it. Well, then you came to the wrong person.

04:31:13.233 --> 04:31:16.867
"The city shall incorporate air dispersion and human

04:31:16.967 --> 04:31:20.467
exposure modeling using best available science and

04:31:20.567 --> 04:31:24.133
data reflective of full permitted or

04:31:24.233 --> 04:31:28.066
licensed operational capacity to inform land use

04:31:28.166 --> 04:31:32.033
decisions, public health assessments, and future policy development

04:31:32.100 --> 04:31:35.900
in areas proximate to petroleum storage and transfer

04:31:36.000 --> 04:31:36.834
facilities."

04:31:37.100 --> 04:31:37.767
Where would that be?

04:31:38.567 --> 04:31:42.433
It would be with 5C13.

04:31:42.600 --> 04:31:46.000
It doesn't take anything away, it asks us to

04:31:46.066 --> 04:31:48.133
incorporate the use of modeling.

04:31:48.500 --> 04:31:52.266
Mr. City Manager, on that statement that she

04:31:52.333 --> 04:31:53.033
just made,

04:31:54.333 --> 04:31:57.934
isn't that similar along the lines of what's been

04:31:58.000 --> 04:31:58.800
going on

04:32:00.433 --> 04:32:02.834
to work on for the last year and a half?

04:32:03.033 --> 04:32:04.767
It was recommended by the CAC.

04:32:05.433 --> 04:32:09.233
Separate from the burst emissions

04:32:09.300 --> 04:32:12.767
work, and maybe is what you're referencing, that's something that the city is

04:32:12.800 --> 04:32:15.900
working with the tank companies and DEP to get

04:32:17.600 --> 04:32:21.400
something stood up. It's already underway. This would be different, though.

04:32:21.467 --> 04:32:25.400
This would specifically call for the HEM modeling, HEM4 model,

04:32:25.467 --> 04:32:26.000
to be

04:32:26.867 --> 04:32:30.200
what the city uses to make determinations and also

04:32:30.967 --> 04:32:32.066
some other things. So it would-

04:32:32.100 --> 04:32:35.400
So this would be a city responsibility, not a business responsibility.

04:32:35.433 --> 04:32:37.667
It would depend on how you'd want to frame it, right?

04:32:37.767 --> 04:32:41.367
Either the city would have to pay for the cost of the modeling, or somehow the

04:32:41.400 --> 04:32:43.033
developer would have to,

04:32:45.467 --> 04:32:48.200
as part of the submission, include that modeling.

